    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T23:25:08Z",
    "body": "PathPilot Hub 2.14.4 (770MX SIM), after 6e246c8: all six probe programs load with **no G-code errors**: face, edge, corner, bore, boss, bore (mm).\n\nThe only messages are travel warnings from the simulator's G54 placement:\n- Z is over by 0.243 in. That is T99's 3.000 in length plus the 50 mm clearance against a G54 Z only 4.73 in below the top of travel.\n- Y is over by 0.37–0.53 in on bore and boss. The inch and mm files are over by the same amount.\nBoth come from the setup, not the post.\n\nStill owed before ready: a no-contact run (G38.2 must stop with an error), and on the real 770MX the back-off after a trip, G55 written by G10 L20 (inch and mm), and the out-of-tolerance stop.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "reactions": {
