    "body": "Marking ready on the contributor's decision, **without real-machine testing**.\n\nWhat was verified:\n- All six probe programs load in PathPilot Hub 2.14.4 (770MX SIM) with no G-code errors. The only warnings are travel warnings from the simulator's G54 placement.\n- Goldens and tests: the probe_tormach suite and `probe_op::the_tormach_post_probes_the_op_with_g38_2`; quick gate green.\n\nNot verified on a control (owed by whoever first runs this on a Tormach):\n1. G38.2 stops with an error when no contact comes. This is the control's documented behaviour.\n2. The G91 back-off right after a trip runs without a \"probe tripped during non-probe move\" error.\n3. `G10 L20 P<n>` writes the target offset correctly in inch and in mm. **Check the offset table after the first probe run before cutting in that offset.**\n4. An out-of-tolerance result shows the (MSG) and stops at M2 without writing the offset.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
