    "body": "Maintainer decision: this stays at needs-rework until the offset write is confirmed on a real control. That means one probe cycle on a Tormach (e.g. 770MX), reading the offset table after `G10 L20 P<n> X[#5420-#190]` in both inch and mm, and checking the G91 back-off after a trip. Hub loading alone isn't enough for a line that can silently write a wrong work offset. Thanks for the careful work and the honest 'not verified' list.",
